+# Implementation notes
+
+## 001 existing flow inspection
+
+Task 001 inspected the current extension points for inbound club messages by email.
+
+### Messaging command flow
+
+- Public API: `web/lib/memba/messaging.ex`
+  - `send_club_message/2` builds a `Memba.Messaging.Commands.SendMessage`, resolves active club recipients through `Memba.Membership.list_active_members_of_club/1`, dispatches to `Memba.Messaging.App`, then delivers each generated `EmailDeliveryRequest` through `Memba.Messaging.EmailDeliveryProvider`.
+  - `deliver_to_provider/1` is synchronous and stops on the first provider error.
+  - Delivery requests use the sender's primary email via `Membership.get_person_primary_email/1`.
+- Command/router/aggregate:
+  - `web/lib/memba/messaging/commands/send_message.ex`
+  - `web/lib/memba/messaging/router.ex`
+  - `web/lib/memba/messaging/message.ex`
+  - Existing message aggregate is identified by `message_id`; duplicate `SendMessage` for the same aggregate returns `{:error, :already_sent}`.
+  - `MessageSent` and `EmailDeliveryCreated` events are emitted in the same stream.
+- Projections:
+  - `web/lib/memba/messaging/projectors/message.ex`
+  - `web/lib/memba/messaging/projectors/email_delivery.ex`
+  - Projectors use `Commanded.Projections.Ecto` with `consistency: :strong`.
+
+### Membership/person email lookup
+
+- Public query API: `web/lib/memba/membership.ex`
+  - `get_person_by_email/1` normalizes input and joins `membership_people` to `membership_person_email_addresses`, so it already finds primary and alternate addresses.
+  - `active_member_of_club?/2` authorizes by resolved `person_id`.
+  - `active_member_of_club_by_email?/2` exists for browser auth and checks primary/alternate projected email rows.
+  - `list_active_members_of_club/1` returns active recipient maps using each person's primary email address only.
+- Email normalization/validation: `web/lib/memba/membership/email_addresses.ex`.
+- Projection schema: `web/lib/memba/membership/projections/person_email_address.ex`.
+
+### Club slug lookup and addressable identity
+
+- Slug helpers: `web/lib/memba/membership/slug.ex`.
+- Club lookup: `Membership.get_club_by_slug/1` normalizes lookup input by trimming and downcasing, then validates the slug.
+- Club-site URL helper: `web/lib/memba_web/club_site.ex`.
+  - Current browser base-domain default is `lvh.me`, configured as `:memba, :club_site`.
+  - The inbound-email domain should be separate from club-site URL generation because the iteration requires default `clubs.memba.io` for email addresses.
+
+### Outbound email provider flow
+
+- Provider port/config:
+  - `web/lib/memba/messaging/email_delivery_provider.ex`
+  - `web/lib/memba/messaging/email_delivery_provider_config.ex`
+  - `web/lib/memba/messaging/email_delivery_request.ex`
+- Providers:
+  - `web/lib/memba/messaging/email_delivery_providers/resend.ex`
+  - `web/lib/memba/messaging/email_delivery_providers/postmark.ex`
+  - `web/lib/memba/messaging/email_delivery_providers/local.ex`
+  - `web/lib/memba/messaging/email_delivery_providers/fake.ex`
+- Runtime provider selection is in `web/config/runtime.exs`; default provider in `web/config/config.exs` is fake.
+- Rejection-email delivery can likely use the same `Memba.Mailer`/Swoosh boundary, but it should not go through `send_club_message/2` because no club message or recipient delivery records should be created for rejected inbound mail.
+
+### Resend webhook and signature handling
+
+- Existing outbound-status webhook controller: `web/lib/memba_web/controllers/resend_webhook_controller.ex`.
+  - It currently handles delivery lifecycle events (`email.delivered`, `email.bounced`, etc.) and maps them to provider-neutral Messaging status-reporting APIs.
+  - It does not parse inbound `email.received` payloads yet.
+- Signature verification: `web/lib/memba_web/resend_webhook_signature.ex`.
+  - Uses Svix headers `svix-id`, `svix-timestamp`, and `svix-signature`.
+  - Verification is enforced by `ResendWebhookController` only when `MembaWeb.ResendWebhookSignature.configured?/0` is true.
+- Raw body caching:
+  - `web/lib/memba_web/cache_body_reader.ex`
+  - `web/lib/memba_web/endpoint.ex` configures `Plug.Parsers` with this body reader, so signature verification can read `conn.assigns.raw_body`.
+- Runtime secret configuration:
+  - `MEMBA_RESEND_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET` is read in `web/config/runtime.exs`.
+
+### Router webhook scope
+
+- `web/lib/memba_web/router.ex`
+  - `/webhooks/postmark` and `/webhooks/resend` are under the JSON `:api` pipeline.
+  - Inbound Resend support can either share `/webhooks/resend` by event type or use an additional route in the same scope; the plan names a dedicated endpoint/parser but also binds use of the existing signature verifier.
+
+### Member dashboard and compose surfaces
+
+- Dashboard:
+  - `web/lib/memba_web/live/member_dashboard_live.ex` delegates rendering to `MembaWeb.PageHTML.club/1`.
+  - Template: `web/lib/memba_web/controllers/page_html/club.html.heex`.
+  - Presentation data: `web/lib/memba_web/member_dashboard_presentation.ex`.
+- Compose:
+  - `web/lib/memba_web/live/member_message_live/new.ex`.
+  - Current compose context assigns `selected_club`, `current_member`, and `active_member_count`.
+- Both surfaces already have selected club data including `slug`, so the upcoming inbound-address helper can be called from presentation/rendering without another lookup.
+
+### Acceptance support
+
+- Shared feature: `acceptance-tests/features/member_message_deliverability.feature`.
+  - Inbound-email scenarios are already present and tagged `@wip`.
+- Browser Cucumber config: `acceptance-tests/cucumber.js`.
+  - Excludes `@wip`.
+- Domain Cucumber config: `web/config/test.exs`.
+  - Excludes `@wip`.
+- Existing browser support:
+  - `acceptance-tests/features/step_definitions/member_message_steps.js`.
+  - `acceptance-tests/features/support/member_message.js`.
+  - Current support covers web compose, outbound test mailbox inspection, delivery status reporting, and no-message failure copy. It does not yet simulate inbound Resend payloads or inspect rejection emails.
+- Existing domain steps:
+  - `web/test/features/step_definitions/messaging_steps.exs`.
+  - Current steps drive `Messaging.send_club_message/2` directly and use `Fake` email provider assertions. No inbound-email steps exist yet.
+
+### Relevant tests to extend later
+
+- Messaging behaviour: `web/test/memba/messaging/send_club_message_test.exs`, `web/test/memba/messaging/message_test.exs`, `web/test/memba/messaging/send_message_dispatch_test.exs`.
+- Resend webhook/signature: `web/test/memba_web/controllers/resend_webhook_controller_test.exs`.
+- Member dashboard/compose UI: `web/test/memba_web/live/member_dashboard_live_test.exs`, `web/test/memba_web/live/member_message_live/new_send_test.exs`.
+- Acceptance config/support: `web/test/features/cucumber_configuration_test.exs`, `acceptance-tests/test/member_message_steps.test.js`.
